 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "22 continues the Paradise of 21: light mood, nothing drawn. 23 carries Al-Muyassar's restriction («ما داموا على الكفر معادين للإسلام») and his meaning of «أولياء» (sharing the Muslims' secrets, taking counsel); kindness and family ties are not forbidden. A house for «آباءكم وإخوانكم», two paths for «استحبوا الكفر على الإيمان». STAGING v4: c1 (22) stays ambient (abiding in Paradise). c2 (23): a home by day; three believers seated at the left (the addressed); on 23:6 three men in dark robes come in from the right (the fathers and brothers named in the verse; only men are drawn). Nothing is acted on the prohibition (23:4-8), on the condition (23:9-13) or on 23:14-19: nobody turns away from his family (Al-Muyassar's restriction: while they stay in disbelief and hostile; kindness is not forbidden). A two-paths plate for preferring disbelief over faith (23:10) stays to the end, so the camera does not hold on the believers while the last words are recited."
 },
